<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
   <meta charset="UTF-8">
   <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
   <title>How It Works - Love Calculator</title>
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="stylesheets/style.css">
</head>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4"></script>

<body>

   <!-- Header -->
   <header>
      <nav>
         <a href="https://mirfeez.github.io/Mirfeez-portfolio" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Menzi</a>
      </nav>

      <a href="/">
         <button class="header-btn">Back to Calculator</button>
      </a>
   </header>

   <!-- Main Section -->
   <div style="margin-top: 3rem;">

      <h1 class=" border-x-3 py-2 border-red-500 rounded text-red-500 mt-4 text-center mb-3 bg-[#221818]">
         💖 How The Love Calculator Works
      </h1>

      <p class="description">
         This calculator does <span class="text-red-500">NOT</span> generate random results.
         It uses a character-based compatibility algorithm.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top:2rem; line-height:1.9; font-size:1.05rem;">
         <div class="border border-zinc-500 rounded-lg mb-11">

            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-2xl m-4">Step 1: Combine Both Names</h3>
            <p class="text-center m-4">
               The two names are joined together and converted to lowercase.
               <br> Example: <strong>Romeo & Juliet → romeojuliet</strong>
            </p>
         </div>

         <div class="border border-zinc-500 rounded-lg mb-11">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-2xl m-4">Step 2: Extract Unique Letters</h3>
            <p class="text-center m-4">
               Only unique alphabetical characters are kept.
               Duplicate letters are ignored.
            </p>
         </div>

         <div class="border border-zinc-500 rounded-lg mb-11">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-2xl m-4">Step 3: Count Letter Frequency</h3>
            <p class="text-center m-4">
               Each unique letter is counted based on how many times it
               appears in the combined name.
            </p>
         </div>

         <div class="border border-zinc-500 rounded-lg mb-11">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-2xl m-4">Step 4: Pair & Reduce</h3>
            <p class="text-center m-4">
               The first and last numbers are added together repeatedly.
               This process continues until only two digits remain.
            </p>
         </div>

         <div class="border border-zinc-500 rounded-lg mb-11">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-2xl m-4">Step 5: Generate Final Score</h3>
            <p class="text-center m-4">
               The final two-digit number becomes the compatibility percentage.
               The same names will always produce the same result.
            </p>
         </div>

      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:2.5rem; text-align:center;">
         <p class="quote" style="background: #221818;">
            “Love may be <span class="font-bold text-lg text-red-500">emotional</span>, but here it’s calculated <span
               class="font-bold text-lg text-red-500">mathematically.</span>😁”
         </p>
      </div>

      <p class="disclaimer" style="margin-top:2rem;">
         ⚠ This calculator is built for fun and entertainment purposes only.
      </p>

   </div>


</body>

</html>